From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:33:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: persistent disk prompt-cache tier, increment 2
 (demote-on-eviction)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LRUPromptCache gains an on_evict(model, tokens, CacheEntry) hook, invoked
wherever it already evicted-and-discarded an entry (insert_cache's two
eviction paths, trim_to's two). The three duplicated eviction blocks
collapse into one _evict_one() helper that calls the hook.

DiskPromptStore gains put_async(): a background daemon thread drains a
queue and writes each demoted entry with the existing (now-synchronous)
put(), so an eviction on the request path never blocks on a disk write.
close() drains the queue and joins the thread, used by both the test and
the server's flush-on-shutdown path (which now closes the store after
flushing the live RAM cache, to also flush any eviction still in flight).

server.py wires prompt_cache.on_evict = disk_store.put_async when
--prompt-cache-dir is set.

New test: test_ram_eviction_demotes_to_disk_asynchronously. All existing
upstream cache tests (23) and this file's prior tests (4) still pass —
the _evict_one refactor is behavior-preserving.

Increment 2 of 3 (NOW.md Phase M1). Disk-lookup-on-RAM-miss is next.
